# Line endings
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every text file is stored in the repository with LF and converted to the
# platform's native form on checkout. Without this, an editor or script that
# rewrites a file with different endings turns a three-line change into a
# whole-file diff and destroys `git blame` for everything before it.
* text=auto

# Shipped deliverables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The single-file builds are checksummed (scripts/generate-checksums.mjs) so a
# user can verify their copy has not been altered. They must survive checkout
# byte for byte - any line-ending conversion would break verification against
# the published .checksums.txt. Git already infers this from their content;
# saying it explicitly stops that inference from silently flipping.
dist/**/*.html -text

# Binary assets Git should never inspect, convert or try to diff.
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.vss binary
